== Content Mods

Mods that add new quests, locations, NPCs, weapons, armor, and world-building content. Every card is verified against its Nexus Mods page (decision register in STATUS.md).

=== Quests & Locations

=== #link("https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/12505")[*Lazarus Awakened*]

A major, fully voiced side questline widely regarded as the best free quest mod for Starfield. Uses the SSNN building in New Atlantis as its starting point.

- *Author:* MinionSquisher
- *Version:* 1.00 / New Version 2.0 (updated 2024-11-22)
- *Dependencies:* None
- *System Impact:* Adds quests, NPCs, locations, and unique rewards
- *Notes:* Use the "New Version 2.0" file — older builds had script-detachment issues. Complete the UC Vanguard line first to avoid spoilers.

=== #link("https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/12506")[*Regrets*]

A self-contained side quest by the Lazarus author: a voiced NPC, a dungeon, environmental storytelling, and unique loot, begun in Akila City.

- *Author:* MinionSquisher
- *Version:* 1.00 (updated 2024-11-20)
- *Dependencies:* None
- *System Impact:* Adds a quest, NPC, dungeon, and rewards
- *Notes:* Touches Akila's Marshal's office and the Waggoner farmhouse — may conflict with mods editing those cells.

=== #link("https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/5824")[*New Landmark Quests - Cut Content Restored*]

Restores discovery quests for the Leaning Tower of Pisa, the Face on Mars, the NASA Launch Facility, and other landmarks that shipped in the files but never got quests.

- *Author:* ConnerRia
- *Version:* 1.35 (updated 2023-10-24)
- *Dependencies:* None
- *System Impact:* Adds quests and objective hooks for otherwise-inaccessible locations
- *Notes:* Old but content-only; quests are started from books at Sinclair's Books in Akila City.

=== #link("https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/11045")[*Dark Universe - Takeover*]

Adds 50 new procedurally placed Spacer military-base POIs, integrated into the radiant quest and bounty systems, so exploration and board missions draw from a much larger pool.

- *Author:* kaosnyrb
- *Version:* 2.1.0 (updated 2026-04-21)
- *Dependencies:* None
- *System Impact:* Adds new locations; integrates with radiant/bounty quests

=== Weapons & Items

=== #link("https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/11770")[*Lodecs Custom Armory (LCA)*]

A lore-friendly weapon pack adding original manufacturers and high-quality firearms — assault rifles, snipers, and particle pistols — that drop and spawn naturally.

- *Author:* lodec
- *Version:* 1.3.3 (updated 2026-05-15)
- *Dependencies:* None
- *System Impact:* Adds weapons to leveled lists and vendors

=== #link("https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/3519")[*Plague's Optics Reimagined*]

Remakes the reflex and holographic sights with 30+ clean, usable reticle options. Uses a FOMOD installer to assign reticles per weapon category.

- *Author:* illbodyPLAGUE
- *Version:* 2.5 (updated 2026-01-09)
- *Dependencies:* None
- *System Impact:* Cosmetic/optics only — no weapon stat changes

=== Armor & Clothing

=== #link("https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/8473")[*Eit Clothiers Plus*]

A large collection of modular clothing — jackets, belts, gloves, glasses, necklaces, and outfits — sold through the EIT Clothiers shop in New Atlantis.

- *Author:* zone79
- *Version:* 2.1 (updated 2025-01-29)
- *Dependencies:* None
- *System Impact:* Adds wearable items to a vendor
- *Notes:* Download the version matching your body mesh (vanilla vs. custom). Pick Zone79 *or* KryoZet gear rather than stacking both, to avoid invisible-body conflicts.

=== Companions & Crew

=== #link("https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/7469")[*The Gang's All Here - Multiple Companions and Crew*]

Lets you travel with multiple companions at once via a control terminal: manage, teleport, and dismiss followers, and tune their commentary.

- *Author:* Aurelianis
- *Version:* 4.3.1 (updated 2026-07-30)
- *Dependencies:* None
- *System Impact:* Changes companion/crew limits
- *Notes:* Dismiss all active crew before installing or updating.
